//
//  kern_sigs.hpp
//  CarrizoRed
//
//  Builds before Sequoia ship AMDRadeonX4000HWLibs stripped (Sonoma 14.8.9: 55 symbols; Sequoia 15.8.1: 9506), so
//  the CAIL/PowerPlay functions CarrizoRed hooks are found by code there. Generated by scripts/siggen.py from the
//  15.8.1 (24H32) KDK and checked against the 14.8.9 (23J631) KDK: every signature finds the same function in both (the
//  occurrence-th match where the code repeats; all 46 sit at the same offset from their 15.8.1 addresses). Pattern
//  bytes under a 0 mask are rel32 / RIP-relative displacements, which move between builds.
//
//  Ventura (13.7.7, 22H722) recompiled CAIL (other register allocation), so its signatures come from its own code:
//  scripts/featmatch.py matched 45 of the 46 functions to 15.8.1's by the constants they use (register numbers,
//  structure offsets) and, for near-identical small functions, by position next to a matched one; scripts/addrsigs.py
//  made the signatures. Monterey (12.7.6, 21H1320, read from the installed system's kexts; no KDK) the same way:
//  41 of 46 matched; the 39 used here leave out PP_Tables_Initialize, PP_ThermalCtrl_Dummy_Initialize, PhwDummy_Initialize,
//  Phw_CommonHwMgr_Initialize and Stoney_SetupASIC (unmatched) and PHM_Initialize / PHM_VerifyHwMgr (weak matches), all
//  trace stages only. Each entry applies to one Darwin major version only (23 Sonoma, 22 Ventura, 21 Monterey), so an
//  occurrence-th match is never taken in a build it wasn't checked against.
//

